:Namespace test_Secure
⍝ TLS / secure-server tests for Jarvis
⍝ Usage:
⍝   From the shell (repository root):  dyalogscript Tests/Secure/run.apls
⍝   From an APL session with #.Jarvis loaded:  #.test_Secure.Run
⍝ Run returns a vector of failure messages; empty means every test passed.
⍝ These tests exercise Jarvis's own TLS configuration logic (CreateSecureParams): that a secure server starts with
⍝ valid certificate files, that the port then speaks TLS (a plain-HTTP request is refused), and that
⍝ mis-configuration produces a clear error. They do NOT perform an encrypted request/response round-trip — that
⍝ depends on the client validating the server certificate chain, which is Conga's job and is best checked manually
⍝ (for example with HttpCommand or a browser, trusting the test CA).
⍝
⍝ Certificates: the tests that need a real certificate use $DYALOG/TestCertificates (override with JARVIS_TEST_CERTS).
⍝ If that folder isn't present, those tests are skipped (reported, not failed).
⍝ Ports: BasePort+1, BasePort+2, ... (8591 and up by default). Set BasePort before Run, or JARVIS_TEST_PORT for run.apls.

    (⎕IO ⎕ML)←1 1
    CRLF←⎕UCS 13 10
    BasePort←8590
    Verbose←1

    TJarvisSource←':Class TJarvis: #.Jarvis' ':Field Public Logged←⍬' '∇ {msg}←{level}Log msg' ':Access public override' 'Logged,←⊂,⍕msg' '∇' ':EndClass'

    ∇ r←Run;tests;t;res
      :Access public
      r←⍬
      :If 9≠#.⎕NC'Jarvis'
          →0⊣r←,⊂'#.Jarvis is not loaded'
      :EndIf
      ⎕FIX TJarvisSource
      Certs←FindCerts
      :If Verbose∧0∊⍴Certs ⋄ ⎕←'(no TestCertificates found; certificate-dependent tests will be skipped)' ⋄ :EndIf
      tests←{⍵/⍨'test_'∘≡¨5↑¨⍵}⎕NL ¯3
      PortsUsed←0
      :For t :In tests
          (Servers Clients)←⍬ ⍬
          :Trap 0
              res←⍎t
          :Else
              res←,⊂'errored: ',⊃⎕DMX.DM
          :EndTrap
          StopAll
          r,←(⊂t,': '),¨res
          :If Verbose
              ⎕←t,': ',(1+0∊⍴res)⊃('FAILED (',(⍕≢res),')')'passed'
              ⎕←⍪res
          :EndIf
      :EndFor
    ∇

⍝ ─── helpers ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    Expect←{⍺:0⍴⊂'' ⋄ ,⊂⍵}
    Contains←{∨/⍺⍷⍵}

    ∇ dir←FindCerts;d
    ⍝ locate a TestCertificates folder (JARVIS_TEST_CERTS, else $DYALOG/TestCertificates); '' if none
      dir←''
      d←2 ⎕NQ'.' 'GetEnvironment' 'JARVIS_TEST_CERTS'
      :If 0∊⍴d ⋄ d←(2 ⎕NQ'.' 'GetEnvironment' 'DYALOG'),'/TestCertificates' ⋄ :EndIf
      :If ⎕NEXISTS d,'/server/localhost-cert.pem' ⋄ dir←d ⋄ :EndIf
    ∇

    ∇ j←NewSecure dummy;cert;key;ca
    ⍝ a (not started) secure server configured with the test certificates
      j←NewServer''
      j.Secure←1 ⋄ j.SSLValidation←64
      j.ServerCertFile←Certs,'/server/localhost-cert.pem'
      j.ServerKeyFile←Certs,'/server/localhost-key.pem'
      j.RootCertDir←Certs,'/ca/'
    ∇

    ∇ j←NewServer dummy
      j←⎕NEW TJarvis
      j.Port←BasePort+PortsUsed←PortsUsed+1
      j.(CodeLocation Paradigm DYALOG_JARVIS_THREAD WaitTimeout)←(MakeApp)'JSON' 'debug' 5000
      j.AllowGETs←1 ⍝ so a plain GET /ping would return 200/pong on a non-TLS server (makes test_PlainRequestRefused meaningful)
      Servers,←j
    ∇

    ∇ app←MakeApp
      app←⎕NS''
      app.⎕FX'r←ping p' 'r←''pong'''
    ∇

    ∇ StopAll;j;c
      :For j :In Servers
          :Trap 0 ⋄ {}j.Stop ⋄ {}j.LDRC.Close j.ServerName ⋄ :EndTrap
      :EndFor
      :For c :In Clients
          :Trap 0 ⋄ {}#.Jarvis.LDRC.Close c ⋄ :EndTrap
      :EndFor
      (Servers Clients)←⍬ ⍬
    ∇

    ∇ got←j PlainGet path;rc;c;w;st
    ⍝ send a plain (non-TLS) HTTP GET to the server and return whatever text came back
      got←''
      (rc c)←2↑j.LDRC.Clt'' 'localhost'j.Port'Text'
      →0↓⍨rc=0
      Clients,←⊂c
      {}j.LDRC.Send c('GET ',path,' HTTP/1.1',CRLF,'Host: localhost',CRLF,'Connection: close',CRLF,CRLF)
      st←⎕AI[3]
      :While 3000>⎕AI[3]-st
          w←4↑(j.LDRC.Wait c 300),4⍴⊂''
          :If 0=⊃w
              :If (⊂3⊃w)∊'Block' 'BlockLast' ⋄ got,←4⊃w ⋄ :EndIf
              :If (⊂3⊃w)∊'BlockLast' 'Closed' 'Error' ⋄ :Leave ⋄ :EndIf
          :ElseIf 100≠⊃w ⋄ :Leave
          :EndIf
      :EndWhile
    ∇

⍝ ─── tests ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    ∇ r←test_SecureStart;j;rc;msg
    ⍝ a secure server starts with valid certificate files
      r←⍬
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(~0∊⍴Certs)Expect'SKIPPED: no TestCertificates'
      j←NewSecure''
      (rc msg)←j.Start
      r,←(rc=0)Expect'secure Start failed: ',⍕msg
      r,←(j.Secure=1)Expect'server should be marked Secure'
    ∇

    ∇ r←test_PlainRequestRefused;j;got
    ⍝ the secure port speaks TLS: a plain-HTTP request does not get a normal response
      r←⍬
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(~0∊⍴Certs)Expect'SKIPPED: no TestCertificates'
      j←NewSecure''
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'secure Start failed'
      got←j PlainGet'/ping'
      r,←(~'pong'Contains got)Expect'a plain HTTP request to the TLS port should not return pong; got ',∊⍕got
      r,←(~'200'Contains got)Expect'a plain HTTP request to the TLS port should not return a 200 response'
    ∇

    ∇ r←test_MissingCertFile;j;rc;msg
    ⍝ a missing ServerCertFile fails Start with a clear message
      r←⍬
      j←NewServer''
      j.Secure←1
      j.ServerCertFile←'/no/such/cert.pem'
      j.ServerKeyFile←'/no/such/key.pem'
      (rc msg)←j.Start
      r,←(rc≠0)Expect'missing ServerCertFile should fail Start'
      r,←((rc≠0)≤'ServerCertFile'Contains msg)Expect'message should mention ServerCertFile; got ',⍕msg
    ∇

    ∇ r←test_MissingKeyFile;j;rc;msg
    ⍝ a valid cert but missing ServerKeyFile fails Start with a clear message
      r←⍬
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(~0∊⍴Certs)Expect'SKIPPED: no TestCertificates'
      j←NewServer''
      j.Secure←1
      j.ServerCertFile←Certs,'/server/localhost-cert.pem'
      j.ServerKeyFile←'/no/such/key.pem'
      (rc msg)←j.Start
      r,←(rc≠0)Expect'missing ServerKeyFile should fail Start'
      r,←((rc≠0)≤'ServerKeyFile'Contains msg)Expect'message should mention ServerKeyFile; got ',⍕msg
    ∇

    ∇ r←test_InvalidCertFile;j;rc;msg;notacert
    ⍝ a ServerCertFile that isn't a certificate fails Start with "Unable to decode"
      r←⍬
      notacert←(2 ⎕NQ'.' 'GetEnvironment' 'DYALOG'),'/TestCertificates/ca/ca-key.pem' ⍝ a real file that is not a usable server certificate
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(~0∊⍴Certs)Expect'SKIPPED: no TestCertificates'
      j←NewServer''
      j.Secure←1
      j.ServerCertFile←notacert
      j.ServerKeyFile←notacert
      (rc msg)←j.Start
      r,←(rc≠0)Expect'a non-certificate ServerCertFile should fail Start'
      r,←((rc≠0)≤'decode'Contains msg)Expect'message should say it could not decode the certificate; got ',⍕msg
    ∇

    ∇ r←test_ServerCertSKINonWindows;j;rc;msg;isWin
    ⍝ ServerCertSKI is only valid on Windows; elsewhere it fails Start with a clear message
      r←⍬
      isWin←'Win'≡3↑⊃#.⎕WG'APLVersion'
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(~isWin)Expect'SKIPPED: running on Windows'
      j←NewServer''
      j.Secure←1
      j.ServerCertSKI←'0123456789ABCDEF0123456789ABCDEF01234567'
      (rc msg)←j.Start
      r,←(rc≠0)Expect'ServerCertSKI on non-Windows should fail Start'
      r,←((rc≠0)≤'Windows'Contains msg)Expect'message should mention Windows; got ',⍕msg
    ∇

:EndNamespace
